{"availability":"available","full":"AtomiJD/jdBasic","name":"jdBasic","description":"BASIC reborn for the AI era: APL-style arrays, SDL3 games, native LLVM compile, Win32 forms, local LLMs, and a built-in MCP server your AI agent can pair-program with.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"C++","stars":18,"forks":1,"created":"2025-07-04T03:10:37Z","updated":"2026-10-12T16:29:49Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.jdbasic.org","topics":["apl","basic","compiler","cplusplus-20","gamedev","interpreter","llm","programming-language","retro-programming","scripting-language"],"demo":"https://jdbasic.org/live/index.html","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T02:09:23.036Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T02:09:23.036Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T02:09:23.036Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:39:34.847Z","stars":18,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-13T02:09:23.036Z","stars":18,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A BASIC you can change while it runs, by hand or through an AI agent.","Claude Code pauses a running game over MCP, rewrites one SUB and lets the game continue with its score and enemies unchanged. Video, 73 seconds.","jdBasic is a BASIC interpreter with a bytecode VM and APL-style arrays. Graphics, GUI, sound, web and local AI are built in. Programs can be compiled to a native .exe, and an MCP server lets an AI agent inspect and change a program without restarting it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomiJD/jdBasic/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c0b642b2c3d61aa437d1b81006248a51ef903a5e487f55a55793600702c5e88c","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:34.987Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:34.987Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A BASIC you can change while it runs, by hand or through an AI agent.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AtomiJD/jdBasic/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"c0b642b2c3d61aa437